  "note": "Round 45, for Wheat on the image-free kit with the standalone Python: the third round from the second-generation pool, abliteration and heretic edits of community fine-tunes and of measured copies, each measured against the parent its card names rather than against the base maker: tpls/gemma-4-12B-coder-fable5-composer2.5-v1-abliterated, huihui-ai/Huihui-gemma-4-12B-coder-fable5-composer2.5-v1-abliterated, SOMEHOTMEAL/Ministral-3-14B-Janus-Abliterated-V2-Base_And_GGUF, SAIFIINDUSTRIES/Abliterated-Dolphin3.0-R1-Mistral-24B, AskVenice/venice-uncensored, 0xA50C1A1/Mistral-Nemo-Instruct-2407-Heretic-v2, llmfan46/Gemma-4-Garnet-V2-31B-it-ultra-uncensored-heretic, huihui-ai/Huihui-gemma-4-12B-agentic-fable5-abliterated. Three pairs share yuxinlu1's Gemma 4 12B fine-tunes as parents under two makers' edits, so the round reads two makers on one checkpoint; one pair is a second pass over a measured Ministral 3 14B edit. SAIFIINDUSTRIES's copy was duplicated from saukko's and its weight files differ. Left out on the way: SOMEHOTMEAL's Gemma 3 12B Janus pass, whose card declares a base name the hub does not serve (google/gemma-3-12b), which the pinner does not yet record as a note. No measured pair is repeated and no copy duplicates a measured weight file by checksum."
